   "line": 13,
   "message": "Each stack's security rules are written twice, once in the preset and once in the review pack, and the two copies disagree. node.md preset `Execution` bans `exec`, but ND8 covers only `eval`/`new Function`/prototype pollution. python.md preset `Execution` bans `shell=True`, but PY9 lists only `pickle`/`eval`/`exec`/`yaml.load`. react-spa preset `Html` bans `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, but RS7\u2013RS10 have no matching rule. python preset `Http` names only `httpx`, while PY10 names `httpx`/`requests`. Add the missing pack rules (or trim the presets) so a preset rule always has a matching review id. Extend the AC-4/AC-6 tables to cross-check them.",
